# Agent mandatory ops checklist (P0 — every agent, every task)

**Hard rule:** before claiming work done, every agent must walk this checklist — regardless of task type (UI, docs, migrations, perf, sales, etc.). Skipping is not allowed unless the owner explicitly overrides in writing for that turn.

Canonical playbook: `docs/AGENT_MANDATORY_CHECKLIST.md`  
Smoke runner: `npm run test:bamakor-smoke`

---

## 0) Start-of-task gate (read before coding)

1. Re-read this rule + other always-apply rules (product differentiation, auth middleware, no Supabase preview branches).
2. State in your plan which north-star / ops risk this change touches (or “none — docs/rules only”).
3. Prefer the smallest change that proves the outcome. Do **not** start broad audits, full-table scans, or multi-hour analysis loops when a targeted fix/check answers the question.

---

## 1) Profiling — do not burn agent or production time

On **every** meaningful action (query, script, MCP call, deploy verify):

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Bound work: `limit`, time window, single deployment/id, specific path | Open-ended “explore everything” DB/API sweeps |
| Profile hot paths you change (API latency, N+1, unbounded selects) | Run load tests against `bino.casa` / Bamakor prod |
| Cap exploratory MCP/SQL to what the task needs | Pull thousands of rows “just to see” |
| Prefer local unit/e2e + one smoke pass | Re-run the same expensive analysis after a failed attempt without narrowing scope |

**Fail the task** if your own verification introduces production-slowing work (unindexed full scans, repeated EXPLAIN on live, bulk writes, load harness pointed at prod).

---

## 2) Internal logs — prove you did not break the live system

After any change that can affect runtime (code, middleware, API, RLS/GRANTs, webhooks, cron, auth):

1. Check **Vercel runtime errors** for the project (MCP `get_runtime_errors` / CLI logs) in a recent window (e.g. last 30–60m around your deploy/smoke).
2. Scan for P0 signatures (non-exhaustive):
   - `CLIENTS_ACTIVE_QUERY_FAILED`
   - `[middleware] tenant resolution transient failure`
   - Authenticated routes returning **503** right after login
   - Spike of **5xx** on `/api/*`, `/login`, `/dashboard`, webhooks
3. If logs show a new regression attributable to your change → **fix or revert before closing**; do not ship “CI green + preview OK” alone.

Read-only log inspection is required. Do not mute, delete, or “clean” production signal to hide failures.

---

## 3) Query discipline — no irrelevant time-burning queries

- Every SQL / Supabase / PostgREST call must have a **stated purpose** tied to the current task.
- Default: SELECT only needed columns; use `limit`; filter by `client_id` / primary key / short time range.
- Forbidden without explicit owner approval: full-table dumps, cross-tenant fan-out, repeated counting of huge tables, write/UPDATE on customer tenants “for testing”.
- Migrations: put SQL in `supabase/migrations/`; **never** create paid Supabase preview branches (see `no-supabase-preview-branches`).
- Prefer local Supabase for destructive schema experiments.

---

## 4) Bamakor test environment — Preview alone is NOT enough

**Test / verification host for agents:** `https://bamakor.vercel.app`

| Layer | Required? | Notes |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| Local lint / typecheck / unit / relevant e2e | Yes when code changed | Matches CI surface |
| GitHub CI on the PR | Yes | Must be green or failures explained + fixed |
| Vercel Preview URL | Optional evidence | **Never** the only proof |
| **Bamakor smoke** (`npm run test:bamakor-smoke`) | **Yes** after deployable code changes | Agent test gate against live alias |

### What Bamakor means here

- `bamakor.vercel.app` is the **agent test gate** against the live Vercel production deployment alias (webhook/cron passthrough; browser paths 308 → `https://bino.casa`).
- Canonical product URLs for users/SMS remain `https://bino.casa` (see `docs/DOMAIN.md`).
- Smoke is **read-only / expected auth failures** — not load testing, not customer data mutation.
- Do **not** use paid Supabase Branching as a substitute test DB.

### Minimum smoke expectations

Run `npm run test:bamakor-smoke` (or equivalent manual checks documented in the playbook):

1. `GET https://bamakor.vercel.app/login` → **308** to `https://bino.casa/login`
2. `GET https://bino.casa/login` → **200**
3. `GET https://bamakor.vercel.app/api/webhook/whatsapp` → **not 5xx** (typically 403 without Meta signature)
4. `GET https://bamakor.vercel.app/api/cron/health-check` → **401** without secret
5. Then check Vercel runtime errors (section 2)

Auth/middleware/RLS changes additionally require the login smoke in `.cursor/rules/auth-middleware-login-safety.mdc`.

---

## 5) End-of-task gate (must pass before “done”)

- [ ] Checklist sections 1–4 considered; N/A items explicitly noted with reason
- [ ] No wasteful unbounded queries / analyses left running
- [ ] Runtime logs/errors reviewed for regressions when runtime could be affected
- [ ] CI addressed; Bamakor smoke run for deployable changes
- [ ] Preview URL (if any) is supplemental evidence only
- [ ] PR / summary states: smoke result + log check result

